{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties","id":1023190,"title":"Homebrew Proximi Dynasties","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-28T04:49:15-08:00","id":1023190,"title":"Homebrew Proximi Dynasties","content":"I was revisiting my ideas for a lineage of Proximi, and I decided to put up this thread to not only share it and ask for critique, but also give a place for people to pitch their own ideas about these magically endowed families. I'll probably be doing some conversions for the Proximi in the Silver Ladder blue book once I've ironed out the Quartermaines.<br /> <br /> Fire away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:52:44-08:00","id":1023192,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Quartermaines</u></b><br /> While its ley lines and High Speech symbols draw much interest in the Awakened world, London is only home to one of many Mysteries that can be found in the United Kingdom. And the Proximi of the Quartermaine Dynasty help seek out and safeguard these wonders. Academics and scientists with high standing in the Mysterium's ranks, their magic is geared towards the study and manipulation of Supernal energy, though a large number are equally blessed in shaping the substance of the Fallen World. While the majority dwell on the British Isles, some Quartermaine Proximi have established themselves in both continental Europe and North America. These Proximi apply their line's duties into mapping out the ley lines and nodes of their home countries, and defending or redirecting them whenever it is needed,<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Ethermancers<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>All Quartermaine Proximi can perceive the mundane and Supernal substance of the world. While they appear normal at first glance, they have unusually vibrant eyes which catch light the same way a cat's or dog's might at night. Should he invoke any one of his Blessings, their eyes give off a bright and intense glow.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Blessings (Forces, Prime, Matter):</b> Forces -- Influence Electricity (o), Influence Fire (o), Control Electricity (oo), Control Fire (oo), Call Lightning (ooo); Matter -- Craftsman's Eye (o), Detect Substance (o), Discern Composition (o), Shaping (oo); Prime -- Dispel Magic (o), Sacred Geometry (o), Supernal Vision (o), Supernal Veil (oo), Wards and Signs (oo), Channel Mana (ooo), Geomancy (ooo), Platonic Form (ooo)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Just as they are attuned to the flow of mundane and Supernal energies around them, all Quartermaines can sense the Abyss whenever it manifests. While some have come to rely on this sense to warn them of their dangers, they nonetheless suffer gravely when in the presence of Abyssal intruders.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> A Quartermaine Proximus suffers from the Disoriented Condition when within sensory range of Abyssal phenomena. This includes not only <i>acamoth</i> and <i>gulmoth</i>, but also Abyssal Verges and active Paradox Conditions, among others.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat: </b>The Quartermaine is virtually helpless against the Abyss' power. Whenever he would suffer harm from being disoriented by his curse, take a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> When a Quartermaine's curse worsens, he becomes a beacon for the Abyss. For the next 24 hours, he counts as a Sleeper witness for all Supernal magic performed in his presence, including his own. In addition, anytime his Blessings are canceled out by Paradox, he takes a point of lethal damage. The Proximus may end the effect early if he performs a successful meditation roll in a Hollow or Supernal Verge.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Architect, leyline surveyor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-07-2017, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:54:40-08:00","id":1023193,"title":"","content":"Proximi don't suffer Paradox, it just shuts down their power and invokes the Severe version of their Curse. I'm not sure that Curse works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:58:21-08:00","id":1023195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023193#post1023193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proximi don't suffer Paradox, it just shuts down their power and invokes the Severe version of their Curse. I'm not sure that Curse works.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a rough draft, but how does this sound?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> Whenever a Quartermaine is struck by the attacks, Influences, or Numina of an Abyssal entity, he suffers an additional point of lethal damage. This damage is resistant, and can only heal naturally. When his Curse worsens, he gains <i>two</i> dice of Paradox risk per Reach. This effect lasts until he either fails a Paradox roll or is not exposed to Abyssal phenomena for a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:26:02-08:00","id":1023202,"title":"","content":"It feels highly circumstantial to me rather than persistently relevant like the curse of the Sisters in the book.<br /> <br /> If I were you I'd focus on figuring out what these guys are first and then worry about the curse instead of doing it backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-28-2016, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:40:53-08:00","id":1023206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023202#post1023202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels highly circumstantial to me rather than persistently relevant like the curse of the Sisters in the book.<br /> <br /> If I were you I'd focus on figuring out what these guys are first and then worry about the curse instead of doing it backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually going by how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> depicted them when I pitched their concept to him - academics and scientists with high-standing in the Mysterium and magic that lets them manipulate natural and supernatural energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:47:01-08:00","id":1023209,"title":"","content":"So their curse should probably be relevant to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:35:20-08:00","id":1023380,"title":"","content":"Perhaps...<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>When a Quartermaine's curse worsens he becomes a beacon for the Abyss. For the remainder of the day the Quartermaine counts as a sleeper witness for all Supernal magic, including his own, performed in his presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T19:51:15-08:00","id":1023554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023380#post1023380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps...<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>When a Quartermaine's curse worsens he becomes a beacon for the Abyss. For the remainder of the day the Quartermaine counts as a sleeper witness for all Supernal magic, including his own, performed in his presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:12:33-08:00","id":1023574,"title":"","content":"Here's my shot at one, just written now.<br /> <br /> The Unstuck<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Laggards<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>The Laggards don\u2019t spend much time socializing with other people from outside their bloodline, there are manifold issues which arise from being a good half-second behind everyone else. In terms of physical appearance, Laggards either seem perpetually rushed and out of time, or utterly serene and content with the pace of their life. Many seek occupations (or lack thereof) which accomodate one who lives their life at a... Different pace.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings: </b>Fate \u2013 Oaths Fulfilled (\u2022), Serendipity (\u2022), Exceptional Luck (\u2022\u2022), Lucky Number (\u2022\u2022), Mind \u2013 Know Nature (\u2022), One Mind, Two Thoughts (\u2022), Perfect Recall (\u2022), Dream Reaching (\u2022\u2022),Incognito Presence (\u2022\u2022), Telepathy (\u2022\u2022), Augment Mind (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Enhance Skill (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Time \u2013 Divination (\u2022), Green Light/Red Light (\u2022), Choose the Thread (\u2022\u2022), Veil of Moments (\u2022\u2022), Shifting Sands (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse: </b>Laggards are ever so slightly unstuck from Time, their minds receiving information a fraction of a second after it should. This can cause manifold issues with appearing slow on the uptake, missing social cues, and difficulties with hand-eye coordination to name a couple.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent</b>: The Unstuck suffer a -1 on all tests involving time management, this rises to -2 when dealing with split-second decisions. This can also impact on social tests, such as when dealing with people who take issue with those who might take almost a second to laugh at an obvious joke. They also suffers a -4 to initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat: </b>The Laggard\u2019s temporal hiccups can cause manifold issues which can put strain on relationships, let alone the harm that can be caused by split second situations of peril. When their \u201cslowness\u201d causes individuals to treat them poorly, or causes them harm take a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>If a Laggard is forced to focus for an extended period on staying \u201cwith it\u201d, fully aware and paying close attention to currently unfolding events, then counterproductively, their temporal dissonance will worsen, forcing them to exist completely out of step with Time. All actions involving interaction with the world suffer a -6 penalty, and their initiative drops to 1. This will persist until they can spend an entire scene in uninterrupted meditation to \u201creset\u201d their clock. If this is forestalled for a further extended period, the Laggard\u2019s mind will pass completely out of the flow of time effectively placing them in a comatose state, which will persist for 24 hours, at which time they awake with the severe condition resolved.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Working with timepieces, relaxing in a serene location where one can lose track of time (public parks are popular).<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concept: </b>Habitual slacker, artisan craftsman, therapist, gardener, tenured university professor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Formatting and so forth 12-29-2016, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T04:54:59-08:00","id":1023681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023206#post1023206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> academics and scientists with high-standing in the Mysterium and magic that lets them manipulate natural and supernatural energy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if their oblation is participation in their own internal academia - they recover mana by preparing research papers and publishing them to internal peer groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T05:46:48-08:00","id":1023700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023681#post1023681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if their oblation is participation in their own internal academia - they recover mana by preparing research papers and publishing them to internal peer groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. Could it be trimmed down, though, to just &quot;participating in academia&quot;? And how about an oblation that's symbolic of their ability to detect and/or manipulate ley lines and nodes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T05:50:21-08:00","id":1023703,"title":"","content":"This looks fun. I have a Proximus family concept that I was working on making into an Art for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a>'s homebrew. The core idea for me was to make some a not terribly evil Legemeton based mage art.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Faustus</u></b><br /> Don't make deals with demons - it never ends well. It's a simple piece of advice, yet it seems like so few mages follow it. Few know this better than the Proximus family known as Faustus. At some point in their history, their progenitor made an unwise pact with a demon of the lower depths - Mephistopheles himself, if the story is to be believed - for knowledge and lordship over both man and spirit. They received all of that and more in the form of awakening, but upon death they were whisked away to some assumed wretched fate. Their children remain, though, eternally a shadow of both the magic received from the pact and the dark fate of being prey to a demon. Through ages past, they've oscillated between being a lighter shade of diabolist cult and demon hunters similar to the Lucifuge. In modern nights, they are spirit summoners working at the behest of the Silver Ladder.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: Daemonologists</b><br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>Least Demons crowd about the descendants of Faustus like flies on rotting meat. Whenever a Faustus Proximus indulges their vice, their shadow seems to laugh, a whiff of brimstone fills the air, surfaces become ice cold, or any number of other tells occur that fill the room with a palpable sense of wrongness.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Blessings (Spirit, Mind, Prime):</b> Spirit -- Know Spirit (o), Gremlins (o), Gossamer Touch (oo), Command Spirit (oo), Spirit Summons (ooo), Bolster Spirit (ooo); Mind -- Know Mind (o), One Mind, Two Thoughts (o), Psychic Domination (oo), Enhance Skill (ooo); Prime -- Dispel Magic (o), Sacred Geometry (o), Supernal Veil (oo), Wards and Signs (oo), Geomancy (ooo), Ephemeral Enchantment (ooo)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> The progenitor of the Faustus line made an unwise bargain with a great being of the lower depths and now their descendants are doomed to repeat that act in miniature until the day their bloodline ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> Whether their vice is pride, addiction, lust, or anything else, it only takes the merest push to set them into their bad habits. A Faustus Proximus may only ever have a single door barring them from acting on their vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat: </b>Should a Faustus be pushed into acting on their own vice in a way that is detrimental to their long term goals, take a beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> As the Faustus's curse deepens, not only does their sin control them, it also depletes them. For the remainder of the day, whenever a Faustus Proximus acts on their vice, they lose a single willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b>The Faustus perform minor evocation rituals of Airy Spirits to generate mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Obsessive Compulsive Sinner, Prideful Daemon Summoner, Mindful Legemeton Scholar<br /> <br /> <br /> Yep. This sucker runs contrary to the rules about arcana selection, but I can't really think of a way to do this concept as I envisioned it while following the letter of the rule. So yeah, this is definitely gonna just remain dubiously rules legal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 12-29-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:11:28-08:00","id":1023711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023703#post1023703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks fun. I have a Proximus family concept that I was working on making into an Art for <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s homebrew. The core idea for me was to make some a not terribly evil Legemeton based mage art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Given what I read, wouldn't it make more sense for them to be a Mastigos lineage? Other than that, though, my only other issue is that they should have 30 dots' worth of Blessings tied to them. You've got one extra dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:16:54-08:00","id":1023714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023711#post1023711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Given what I read, wouldn't it make more sense for them to be a Mastigos lineage? Other than that, though, my only other issue is that they should have 30 dots' worth of Blessings tied to them. You've got one extra dot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely on both counts. Their Obrimos distinction is largely the relic of their origin as something for the PenDragon Hacks. The main reason I went for Obrimos though was because I wanted to make a PenDragonBrew art that was heavily drawing on the &quot;Fire and Brimostone, Solomonic Summoning, Evocation in the name of Arch Angels and the Lord God&quot; style summoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:18:04-08:00","id":1023715,"title":"","content":"Faustus: Two of the arcana blessings have the be tied to a Path, so if they're Obrimos they should be Prime, Forces and Spirit or Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:40:26-08:00","id":1023726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023715#post1023715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faustus: Two of the arcana blessings have the be tied to a Path, so if they're Obrimos they should be Prime, Forces and Spirit or Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the Sisters have Spirit, Life, and Fate despite being Acanthus? That said, when I did the Quartermaines, I went with that old rule in the Silver Ladder blue book that 20 of the Blessing dots should be in Primary Arcana spells. Granted, it's probably not the case in 2E, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:48:04-08:00","id":1023730,"title":"","content":"While diving even deeper into homebrew territory, what about Proximus Dynasties that trade breadth for depth? Like loosing access to one arcana entirely (so they only have 2) in exchange for being able to reach higher in the other two (total dots between Blessings would remain at 30)? Could even go further and have one arcana able to have 5-dot Blessings... but that's the only one they have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:53:41-08:00","id":1023734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023726#post1023726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't the Sisters have Spirit, Life, and Fate despite being Acanthus? That said, when I did the Quartermaines, I went with that old rule in the Silver Ladder blue book that 20 of the Blessing dots should be in Primary Arcana spells. Granted, it's probably not the case in 2E, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're Thyrsus and have Life, Spirit and Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:14:30-08:00","id":1023742,"title":"","content":"Good work with the Faustus. I can clearly imagine John Constantine as one of those magnificent bastards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:24:25-08:00","id":1023812,"title":"","content":"Because my last Proximus line was dubiously legal, here is a line of villain Proximi that should actually follow all the rules. Basically, a stereotypically evil frat house and their conniving politician parents.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Fire and Brimstone Brothers</u></b><br /> <br /> There are many colorful rumors thrown about regarding the Fire and Brimstone Brothers. Despicable patriarchs bound by a minor Egregore; psycho trustafarians roiling with magical madness; or, most accurately, a magical Old Boys' Club in its purest sense. The Proximus blessing of the Brimstone Brothers passes from father to son, skips women entirely, and changes with age. They start off hot, violent, and focused on debauchery, but only ever the sort of debauchery that is tacitly accepted as &quot;boys being boys&quot; in their culture. As the years go by, Fire and Brimstone Brothers burn lower and start to focus on grand machinations that can be achieved with Fate and Time blessings. Old Sports love hierarchy and order. As such, their ranks are split between adherents of the Silver Ladder and the Seers of the Throne. Regardless of their leanings in awakened politics, Brimstone Brothers are always viciously dogmatic and conservative about changes to their group's doctrine. Perhaps the rumor they do the most to deny is that the Fire and Brimstone Brothers began as homunculi created in the image of nobility by a nameless archmaster. But the jealous do spread such nasty rumors about their betters.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: Old Sports</b><br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>The Fire and Brimstone Brothers, no matter how hard they try, always seem artificial. Their eyes seem glazed, their skin seems overly made up, and they leave an overall impression of being a stock caricature more than a human being.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <b>Blessings (Time, Fate, Forces):</b> Time -- Divination (o), Perfect Timing (o), Momentary Flux (o), Choose the Thread(oo), Veil of Moments (oo), Temporal Summoning (ooo), Bolster Spirit (ooo); Fate -- Quantum Flux (o), Serendipity (o), Fools Rush In (oo), Sworn Oaths (ooo), Superlative Luck (ooo); Forces -- Kinetic Efficiency (o), Kinetic Blow (oo), Control Fire (oo), Control Sound (oo), Telekinetic Strike (ooo)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> The Fire and Brimstone Brothers are victims of magical compelled to keep of appearances and adhere to group-think for their specific group.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> Whichever social group the Brimstone Brother associates with most, their laws and, far more importantly, their norms are sacrosance to the Proximus. Whenever they violate one, they gain the Guilty condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat: </b>Should a Fire and Brimstone Brother earn ostracism from their peers for breaking a social taboo, they gain a beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>Social suicide takes on a whole new meaning as the Old Sport's proximi curse deepens. In addition to gaining the Guilty condition, the proximus also suffers the Sickened tilt until such a time as they can regain their social standing.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Revelry for the young and machinating for the old.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Black-Sheep Among Wolves, Repressed Athlete, Politician With a Veritable Crypt in his Closet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 12-29-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:33:55-08:00","id":1023817,"title":"","content":"I'd leave the Sickened Condition until such time as they can regain their social standing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:39:55-08:00","id":1023823,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I've edited it to include that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:17:48-08:00","id":1024009,"title":"","content":"So, what about a lineage whose curse is that they're all locked into Vassalage with something? The Severe version of it could be that they have their soul taken from them until they can redeem themselves to their master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:45:33-08:00","id":1024051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1023734#post1023734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're Thyrsus and have Life, Spirit and Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That must be an errata I missed, then, since I have an old copy. The Sisters of the Mountain were written as Acanthus in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1024009#post1024009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about a lineage whose curse is that they're all locked into Vassalage with something? The Severe version of it could be that they have their soul taken from them until they can redeem themselves to their master.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Myrmidons have something along those lines. And so does the homebrewed Pendragon Dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-29-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:04:50-08:00","id":1024058,"title":"","content":"I did <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/916681-proximi-family-guess-what-i-ve-been-reading-the-house-atreides\">the Atreides</a> as a Proximi dynasty a while back - they build off of one of Dataweaver's Paths, because I needed Life, Mind, and Time, and there is <i>literally</i> no way it would have worked otherwise.<br /> <br /> I do have an idea for another one, though - I'll post it when I have it in a presentable state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:01:32-08:00","id":1024290,"title":"","content":"I got bunch of them from 1E times - just need to review them to 2E format. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:28:03-08:00","id":1027634,"title":"","content":"What about a Proximus &quot;Dynasty&quot; that represents the Proximus as a &quot;cyborg&quot; - their Blessings are &quot;cybernetic augmentations&quot;, their Curse a natural drawback of their experimental systems, etc. Really, they are a Proximus, just like any other and they are doing magic, just like any other, but the spin and message is that this is advanced tech (perhaps as an experiment to get around observer influenced Paradox).<br /> <br /> Ideas on the Arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:53:09-08:00","id":1027654,"title":"","content":"Forces, Matter and take your pick of Death or Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:54:51-08:00","id":1027655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1027634#post1027634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a Proximus &amp;quot;Dynasty&amp;quot; that represents the Proximus as a &amp;quot;cyborg&amp;quot; - their Blessings are &amp;quot;cybernetic augmentations&amp;quot;, their Curse a natural drawback of their experimental systems, etc. Really, they are a Proximus, just like any other and they are doing magic, just like any other, but the spin and message is that this is advanced tech (perhaps as an experiment to get around observer influenced Paradox).<br /> <br /> Ideas on the Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that theit parent path would be Moros. Theit use of Matter and Death keeps their cybernetics working while staving off decay. Perhaps they would use Forces or Life as their third Arcana. Forces would show their ability to manipulate tech whike Life would show how their augmentatons elevate their physical forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:07:39-08:00","id":1027663,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Tsuchimikado</u></b><br /> For 1,000 years, the Tsuchimikado Family has served as lords and stewards to Kyoto. Its members nurture an inherent connection to the spirits, while the Proximi among them have accomplished some of the greatest feats of spirit magic. One of these is their fabled mirror city - a magical construction that is said to lie at the heart of Kyoto's spiritual reflection. In modern nights, the Tsuchimikado are in a conflicted position, as they have blood ties not only to the Gin no Hashigo, but also to the hunter conspiracy known as the Aki Ten.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> While largely mundane in looks, all Tsuchimikado have a large dragon birthmark somewhere on their bodies. This birthmark is adorned, in turn, with a mixture of High Speech symbols, which vary between individual Proximi.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Omnyoji<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Thyrsus<br /> <b>Blessings (Fate, Life, Spirit): </b>Fate -- Interconnections (o), Oaths Fulfilled (o), Quantum Flux (o), Shifting the Odds (oo), Warding Gesture (oo), Grave Misfortune (ooo), Monkey's Paw (ooo), Sworn Oaths (ooo); Life -- Speak with Beasts (o), Web of Life (o); Spirit -- Exorcist's Eye (o), Know Spirit (o), Cap the Well (oo), Channel Essence (oo), Reaching (ooo), Spirit Summons (ooo)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse: </b>The Tsuchimikado sticks out like a sore thumb to spirits, who instinctively know that he can assist them with their troubles. While this is a nuisance when it comes to squires and knights, it becomes a real danger when higher-ranking spirits are involved.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> All spirits treat the Proximus as having the Resonant Condition, and gain a bonus equal to their Rank on all rolls made to track him down.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat: </b>The Tsuchimikado are lords between the mortal and spirit worlds, and this comes before any other facet of their lives. If the Proximus is forced to go out of his way to assist or seal a spirit, take a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b> When the Tsuchimikado succumbs to Paradox or neglects to fulfill his duties, he becomes mentally drained. Spirits of Rank 3 or higher may command obedience from the Onmyoji, and make requests of him that must be fulfilled. If he refuses, he does not regain Willpower from sleeping, and loses a Willpower point after a number of days equal to his Resolve. This lasts until the task is accepted, the spirit is made to rescind its command, or a full lunar cycle has passed.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Cleaning a shrine, Interacting with spirits, Qigong exercises, Reciting ku-ji<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts: </b>Hallucinating schizophrenic, natural onmyoji, spirit warden <hr />As one of the larger Proximi Dynasties, the Tsuchimikado have a number of branches that exhibit different Blessings. All, however, are united by a common affinity for Fate and the spirits, and a shared Curse.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Alternative Blessings:</u></b> <br /> <br /> <b>Fate </b>-- Exceptional Luck (oo), Shifting the Odds (oo)<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b> -- Analyze Life (o), Body Control (oo), Heightened Senses (oo)'<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b> -- Command Spirit (oo), Gossamer Touch (oo), Opener of the Way (oo), Bolster Spirit (ooo), Place of Power (ooo)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":".  Added Oblations and Character Concepts 09-26-2017, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:10:44-08:00","id":1027670,"title":"","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a>'s Tsuchimikado. I'll be returning to this every now and then to fill out the empty sections of the write-up. On a semi-related note, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, this is a tie-in to the Shattered Mirror sidebar for your Aki Ten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:19:34-08:00","id":1027676,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> I like it, but that Severe Curse needs work. Perhaps they suffer a Hex of some kind until they get a spirit to &quot;forgive&quot; them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:31:50-08:00","id":1027685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1027676#post1027676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> I like it, but that Severe Curse needs work. Perhaps they suffer a Hex of some kind until they get a spirit to &quot;forgive&quot; them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a work-in-progress. But your suggestion actually can work. How about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> If the Tsuchimikado is struck by Paradox or neglects his duties, Fate will see fit to punish him with a Hex. If it is the former, the Hex's Potency is equal to the dots of the canceled Blessing. If it is the latter, the Potency is equal to the Rank of whichever spirit was offended by the Proximus. Multiple Hexes can stack with one another, and their total Potency is reduced at a rate of one per week. If the Tsuchimikado fulfills a service for or makes proper reparations to a spirit, he may subtract its Rank in Potency from a Hex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-06-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T16:39:40-08:00","id":1027915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1027670#post1027670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a>'s Tsuchimikado. I'll be returning to this every now and then to fill out the empty sections of the write-up. On a semi-related note, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, this is a tie-in to the Shattered Mirror sidebar for your Aki Ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fairly different take than my Tsuchimikado, but works well enough. Though it might interest you to know that I altered the Tsuchimikado curse in 2e. They now have an effective Spirit Rank and must show respect and obedience to Spirits (and other Tsuchimikado) who out rank them.<br /> <br /> Edit: By core rules it might look like...<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>When the Tsuchimikado succumb to Paradox they succumb to the Shadow. Spirits of Rank 3 or higher may command obedience from the Onmyoji, and make requests of them that must be fulfilled. This state lasts until they receive a task from one such spirit, or until the moon completes one full cycle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I should really finish the 2e doc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-06-2017, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T18:16:32-08:00","id":1027960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1027915#post1027915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fairly different take than my Tsuchimikado, but works well enough. Though it might interest you to know that I altered the Tsuchimikado curse in 2e. They now have an effective Spirit Rank and must show respect and obedience to Spirits (and other Tsuchimikado) who out rank them.<br /> <br /> Edit: By core rules it might look like...<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>When the Tsuchimikado succumb to Paradox they succumb to the Shadow. Spirits of Rank 3 or higher may command obedience from the Onmyoji, and make requests of them that must be fulfilled. This state lasts until they receive a task from one such spirit, or until the moon completes one full cycle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I should really finish the 2e doc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks x3<br /> I'll probably go with this take on the Curse, albeit with some tweaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-07-2017, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:59:58-08:00","id":1029484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1027915#post1027915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should really finish the 2e doc...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, no pressure but I'm always super down for more of your homebrew. It's the only way my friends and I can play Mage these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T05:23:12-08:00","id":1029559,"title":"","content":"Tentative update to the persistent and severe versions of the Tsuchimikado Curse, as well as additional info. <hr /><br /> <b>Persistent:</b> The Proximus can see, hear, and touch spirits in Twilight, and can be touched by them in turn. Furthermore, all spirits treat him as having the Resonant Condition, and gain a bonus equal to their Rank on all rolls made to track him down.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe: </b>When a Tsuchimikado suffers Paradox or refuses a command given to him by a spirit of Rank 3 or above, he begins to grow mentally drained. He does not regain Willpower from sleeping, and loses a Willpower point every week. This lasts until the task is completed, the spirit is made to rescind its command, or a full lunar cycle has passed.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Cleaning a shrine, Interacting with spirits, Qigong exercises, Reciting ku-ji<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Hallucinating schizophrenic, natural onmyoji, spirit warden","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-10-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T18:17:37-07:00","id":1068962,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Atlantis, Ltd.</b></u><br /> There are some who have been given a second chance. Maybe they were saved from being a cripple. Maybe it was from being merely mediocre. Regardless, they were deemed a suitable candidate and went through The Procedure. Now they've had their bodies enhanced with technological enhancements that are nearly beyond belief - provided they can prevent straining their abilities too much, or drawing undesired attention. At least, that's what the company tells them. It far easier to accept than &quot;channeling magical symbols to alter reality&quot;.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Most prefer full body coverings and thicker clothes, the better to conceal their scars and the signs of their gifts. Those self-same gifts make portions of their bodies seem mechanical, artificial, and &quot;cybernetic&quot;.<br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Augmented, 'Borgs<br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Blessings (Forces, Prime, Life):</b> Forces - <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kinetic Efficiency (\u2022), Nightvision (\u2022), Receiver (\u2022), Tune In (\u2022), Control Sound (\u2022\u2022), Environmental Shield (\u2022\u2022), Invisibility (\u2022\u2022), Kinetic Blow (\u2022\u2022), Transmission (\u2022\u2022), Zoom In (\u2022\u2022); Prime - Pierce Deception (\u2022); Life - Analyze Life (\u2022), Web of Life (\u2022), Body Control (\u2022\u2022), Heightened Senses (\u2022\u2022), Honing the Form (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Knit (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <b>Curse:</b> Though of great assistance, and in some cases even healing other wounds, the &quot;artifical&quot; nature of their gifts cause their biology to have an adverse reaction.<br /> <b>Persistent: </b>Maintaining their artificial components takes certain metals and uncommon chemicals (worth at least Resources \u2022\u2022) a month - being deprived of adequate supplies triggers the same effect as Starvation. Additionally, the personal nature of their gifts means they can largely only affect themselves - attempting to use their non-Knowing Blessings upon another target aggravates their Curse.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> If the lack of necessary materials forces the character to endanger themselves to acquire them.<br /> <b>Severe:</b> Their body start rejecting their mechanical parts, causing 1 Resistant Lethal damage.<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Performing maintenance upon their cybernetic parts, hooking up to low level current, eating high energy foods<br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Disabled vet, experimental procedure volunteer, crash survivor, street samurai<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments:</u> Thought up after playing too much Shadowrun and Deus Ex. The idea here is that the spells replicate various cybernetic implants. Forces for kinetic boosts to strength and interaction with the electromagnetic spectrum. Life picks up the healing, armor, and physical attribute enhancement. Prime is there just because, really - I didn't have room to add the other abilities that would have made more sense later in the Arcana. The other ideas here is that these Proximi might be <i>made</i>, not &quot;born&quot;, and that the party responsible wants to delude them into thinking their powers are technological in nature. Whether this will have any effect on Paradox and secrecy is debatable.]<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Tremere-lite]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Description]<br /> <b>Appearance:</b><br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Parent Path:</b> Moros</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessings (Death, Matter, Prime):</b> Death - Sever Soul (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Devouring the Slain (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Without a Trace (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">), Suppress Aura (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Soul Jar (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Soul Armor (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Soul Marks (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">); </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter - Windstrike (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Hidden Hoard (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Craftsman's Eye (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">); Pr</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ime - Dispel Magic (\u2022), Word of Command (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Cloak Nimbus (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Supernal Veil (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Channel Mana (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curse: </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Persistent:</b> [Detachment issue?] [Can't gain Willpower from Virtue or Vice without another Soul attached?]<br /> <b>Beat:</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Severe:</b> [Soul Loss?]<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> [Researching a potential victim?] [Furthering one of the current soul's Aspiration?]<br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b><br /> [<u>Comments:</u> So, the idea here is to see how paired down you can get for the basic idea of the Soul-Reaping Tremere. Sever Soul is only Death 3 - within the ability for a Proximus Dynasty to have. The big question is &quot;what else&quot;? The 30 Blessing Dots limit really restricts what they can fully do, so I went for stealth or versatility when possible. Without a Trace, Suppress Aura, Cloak Nimbus, and Supernal Veil are for hiding what they are. Hidden Hoard is for keeping their Soul Jars concealed. Windstrike is a versatile attack spell (if they are willing to Reach for the Tilts), and Dispel Magic a decent counter. Word of Command and Channel Mana lets them utilize others' Imbued Items to expand their abilities even more.]</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-31-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:00:25-07:00","id":1071257,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any pointers on what I can name and use as the curse for the Diet Tremere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:48:31-07:00","id":1071354,"title":"","content":"I have a Proximi dynasty I've worked on, and I even have a general idea for the curse, in the sense that I know what I want to happen to them, but I'm not sure how to mechanically pull it off. It's rather frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T13:04:54-07:00","id":1071387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1071354#post1071354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a Proximi dynasty I've worked on, and I even have a general idea for the curse, in the sense that I know what I want to happen to them, but I'm not sure how to mechanically pull it off. It's rather frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you have so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:45:52-07:00","id":1071561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1071387#post1071387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you have so far?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Hidden Judgement Cult <br /> <br /> <br /> Description: A group with deep roots, this Proximi line began by seeming chance. In Europe, a cult in the control of a number of Seer factions seemed to stumble upon a ritual or rite that could empower someone to the status of Proximi. They exploited it for some time, creating four or five Proximi in rituals that sometimes drew negative attention onto the group, which they carefully deflected with their powers, blaming others and leading to a number of mobs forming, chaos, blood in the streets. And then, just as suddenly, just as inexplicably, the ritual stopped working.<br /> <br /> Ever since then the cult has shepherded the charmed bloodline of five people (none related) who intermarried in the hopes of keeping the power within them. They have fallen almost entirely under the control of the Seers, and to this day the Proximi are the property of various Seer Ministries, most recently, over the last century, Panopticon, who has found plenty of use for their abilities, and has made sure that they keep as secret and quiet as possible, this strange cult-family harsh and judgmental to outsiders, and given to inbreeding and other strange habits, their own rituals warped by the centuries into superstitions, despite their access to the Truth.<br /> <br /> They specialize in finding out secrets, wracking their enemies with guilt and whipping up crowds to lynch or destroy the lives of those they judge unworthy. This very judgement is a two-way street, and their Curse exposes them to considerable risks, risks that they must face if they wish to use their powers. <br /> <br /> Nickname: Scolds. <br /> Parent Path: Mastigos<br /> Blessings: (Mind, Space, Spirit)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind--Know Nature (*), Mental Scan (*), Emotional Urging (**), First Impression (**), Enlightened Will (***) Read the Depths (***), Befuddle (***) [14]<br /> <br /> Enlightened Will (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> <br /> The mage grants the subject an additional Vice, as the Vice-Ridden Merit: &quot;Succeeding on invested actions.&quot;<br /> +1 Reach: For a point of Mana, mundane actions where the subject spends Willpower have the rote quality.<br /> +2 Reach: For a point of Mana, the subject automatically succeeds on uncontested mundane actions where they spend Willpower. On contested mundane actions, they add effective successes equal to Potency if they rolled at least one success.<br /> <br /> Space--Correspondence (*), Isolation (*), Borrow Threads (**), Scry (**), Iron Chains (**), Perfect Sympathy (***) [11]<br /> <br /> Iron Chains (Space \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Practice: Shielding<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Socialize, Politics, Empathy<br /> This spell target a sympathetic connection. As long as the spell endures, this link cannot be altered in strength or quality by mundane events: he'll remain in the friendzone, she'll never manage to get a divorce, this kid will never get bored of his favorite toy.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell can take two targets not connected by a sympathetic link. It prevents any meaningful relationship to develop, maintaining their sympathy null.<br /> +1 Reach: Even the supernatural can't break the Iron Chain. Any attempt to alter the sympathetic connection provoke a Clash of Will.<br /> <br /> Spirit--Exorcist\u2019s Eye (*), Know Spirit (*), Channel Essence (**)*<br /> <br /> * I was considering Command Spirit, but perhaps it'd be best for them to be all carrot and stick? <br /> <br /> And here's the part where I have an idea but am not sure how to work with it:<br /> <br /> Curse: Each Scold finds that for all that their traditional purpose was to find and expose sinners to be cast out, that their own sins drag behind them. If he does not indulge in the sins and vices that she finds in the sick human minds that he so judges, it will come back to cripple him. And each new person is a new vice, a trail of guilt that they must obscure and hide. <br /> <br /> Persistent: Any time they use a Blessing on someone else, they automatically gain that person\u2019s vice, switching for either one day or when they properly fulfill the vice, at which point they are open to take on another vice. Willpower adds only one dice to any action to try to resist indulging the vice, no matter the consequences. <br /> <br /> Beat: ???<br /> <br /> Severe: If they go one week without having fulfilled a vice that is their own, without having indulged in a sin, if they refuse to give into the sudden, powerful urges, then she finds that that is all she has now. She can no longer add willpower to a roll to resist indulging in a vice, and each new person she uses her powers on ADDS another vice, each of which tugs and screams at her to be indulged, no matter what. She only turns back when she successfully fulfills every single one of her vices in a single day.<br /> <br /> Oblations: Revealing a damaging secret shame of someone else\u2019s, gossiping for an extended period of time about someone else, driving someone to act in a manner against their moral code, without using magic. <br /> <br /> ******<br /> <br /> The basic idea with the Curse is that it relates to their nature. They find out hidden sins and manipulate people for the Seers, but in turn they're driven to all the same sins. The adulterer that they blackmail means that suddenly they feel the urge to cheat, the drunkard they frame for a crime with magic suddenly has them thirsty and desperate for a drink, and if they deny it, then it gets worse for them. Maybe via conditions or something? Not sure how to make it work. Vices clearly would get too cluttered, whereas Conditions might make sense, as long as it's denied as a source of EASY beats. Whatever causes the Beat would have to be something unrelated to resolving the Condition, which I think wouldn't be rewarded. The Beats would be for, &quot;When indulging in vices/sins leads you to fuck things up&quot; or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T20:06:00-07:00","id":1071566,"title":"","content":"Just a note about Iron Chains. It should lead to Clash of Wills by default without requiring a Reach. I get that it already has an effect, but CoW is triggered whenever a supernatural effect is directly opposed by another supernatural effect (unless one of them has specific rules for resolving the situation) so it wouldn't really be a second effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T11:28:01-07:00","id":1072111,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Investigators]<br /> [Something, something, born seekers of truth and the bringers to light of secrets]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Appearance:</b><br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Snoops, Counsels, Gumshoes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Parent Path:</b> Acanthus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessings (Fate, Time, Prime):</b> Fate - </span></span>Warding Gesture (\u2022\u2022), Shifting the Odds (\u2022\u2022), Lucky Number (\u2022\u2022), Fools Rush In (\u2022\u2022), Serendipity (\u2022), Quantum Flux (\u2022), Oaths Fulfilled (\u2022), Interconnections (\u2022)<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">; Time - </span></span>Temporal Summoning (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Shifting Sands (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Choose the Thread (\u2022\u2022), Postcognition (\u2022), Momentary Flux (\u2022), Divination (\u2022)<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">; Prime - </span></span>Words of Truth (\u2022\u2022), Cloak Nimbus (\u2022\u2022), Supernal Vision (\u2022), Pierce Deception (\u2022), Dispel Magic (\u2022)<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curse: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Something that keeps them focused on solving mysteries? Or makes them keep their word or speak true?]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Persistent:</b> [Something about Obsession to unsolved mysteries?] [Tie into their Virtue, so they can't let a case rest that pulls at their higher self?] [Addicted to Mysteries - as in, they have the Persistent Addicted Condition for Clues from the Investigation system]<br /> <b>Beat:</b> [When they get &quot;beat&quot;, like what often happens to noir investigators?]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Severe:</b> [???]<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> [Looking at an evidence/connection board?]<br /> <b>Character Concepts: </b>Mystic PI, Busybody that can't leave well enough alone, Reluctant investigator in way over their head<br /> [<u>Comments:</u> So, this was one of many different takes on a natural Investigator type character for a Proximus Dynasty. Warding Gesture keeps them on target. Oaths Fulfilled can be used to verify future actions, or as a tracker. Other Fate spells streamline investigations, and give them a &quot;lucky&quot; break. Time spells let them examine objects and a scene long after evidence and clues would be gone. Cloak Nimbus lets them go &quot;under cover&quot;, Words of Truth lets their evidence be taken meaningfully, and Dispel Magic lets them bypass magic blocking their way.</span></span>]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T19:06:52-07:00","id":1074458,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. What does everyone think about treating an Attainment as one of the Blessings (thus, only those up to 3 dots)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T21:14:34-07:00","id":1074503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1074458#post1074458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. What does everyone think about treating an Attainment as one of the Blessings (thus, only those up to 3 dots)?</div> </div> </div> </div>3-dot Attainments are Targeted Summoning, so I doubt it'll be of use for Proximi. Unless they can already summon Supernals and I missed it.<br /> <br /> 1- and 2-dot Attainments are nice, but how would we figure out the Proximus' Arcana ratings for things like Counterspell and Mage Armor? Equal that of the highest-ranked Blessing they have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T22:53:47-07:00","id":1074526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1074503#post1074503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3-dot Attainments are Targeted Summoning, so I doubt it'll be of use for Proximi. Unless they can already summon Supernals and I missed it.<br /> <br /> 1- and 2-dot Attainments are nice, but how would we figure out the Proximus' Arcana ratings for things like Counterspell and Mage Armor? Equal that of the highest-ranked Blessing they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they can Supernal Summon, but having that Attainment might allow it. As for effect Arcana rating, what about fixed at the dot of the Attainment (or Willpower for the Clash, since that is their spellcasting pool).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T23:57:03-07:00","id":1074539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1074526#post1074526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think they can Supernal Summon, but having that Attainment might allow it. As for effect Arcana rating, what about fixed at the dot of the Attainment (or Willpower for the Clash, since that is their spellcasting pool).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, haven't looked at the summoning rules for awhile, so no ideas on how it'll turn out. The other issue seems nicely solved, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T17:20:02-07:00","id":1081189,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Anyone have any ideas on how to set up the Curse for a &quot;Scelesti&quot; Proximus Dynasty? I'm thinking something that forces them to trigger/flirt with Paradox, without shooting itself in the foot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T06:55:15-07:00","id":1099810,"title":"","content":"Some other ideas I am playing around with:<br /> <br /> Basing the degree of the Curse or Appearance on the number of Blessing dots they have. That gives a range of 1 to 30. Example: <b>Atlantis, Ltd.</b> become visibly more cybernetic as their power grows, like [Blessing dots]% of their body is noticeably &quot;artificial&quot; (so, barely visible at 1 dot, up to 30% with all Blessings taken).<br /> <br /> Use the basic template for an &quot;anti-Proximus&quot; - basically, instead of casting their Blessings, they use them as a prerequisite for countering those spells that others cast.<br /> <br /> Using the Curse to enforce certain casting methodologies and styles. Like making a Gunslinger-like Dynasty only use Aimed Spells, or another unable to cast at quicker than Ritual length, or another having their Forces restricted to Cold effects.<br /> <br /> A Merit to let Proximi cast spells in their Blessing Arcana, but not listed as their Blessings, likely with many limitations or requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:48:15-07:00","id":1105763,"title":"","content":"Feedback would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Walkers On Nails<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Danger Magnets<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Walkers On Nails often have scars from glancing blows they dodged just in the nick of time. The soles of their feet often display hardened textures similar to tree bark, stone or iron. When invoking their Blessings, they seem to move with preternatural agility, making them look like a blur but also making their steps release strange sounds that attract danger to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings:</b> Fate \u2013 Quantum Flux (1), Reading The Outermost Eddies (1), Serendipity (1), Exceptional Luck (2), Fools Rush In (2), Shifting The Odds (2), Warding Gesture (2), Superlative Luck (3)<br /> <br /> Time \u2013 Divination (1), Green Light/Red Light (1), Momentary Flux (1), Postcognition (1), Hung Spell (2), Tipping The Hourglass (2), Veil Of Moments (2)<br /> <br /> Space \u2013 Correspondence (1), Outward And Inward Eye (1), Break Boundary (2), Scrying (2)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse: </b>The Walkers are never too close or too far away from Fate, always trying to escape from trouble or get into it. This makes their lives unstable to say the least, but makes them valuable as scouts and spies, for conflict of all sorts gravitates towards them before other people.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> The Walkers suffer a -2 on all rolls to avoid drawing attention to themselves or avoiding harm from incidental sources.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> If forced to get into a situation where they\u2019ll draw attention to themselves or risk considerable harm, the Walker gets a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> Danger comes to Walkers one way or another. If they avoid situations where they would suffer the Persistent Condition, Fate conspires to create an Environmental Tilt with them as the epicenter, or apply Personal Tilts to as many people as possible, including the Walker.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Juggling sharp objects, Actually walking on nails, drinking poisons, Getting lost in a bad part of town or in the woods, Extreme Sports<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Adrenaline Junkie, Reluctant Explorer, Brave Martyr","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:14:45-07:00","id":1111895,"title":"","content":"So, what would a werewolf-y Proximus line look like? Life (for senses and transformation) and Spirit (duh) are a given, but what other Arcana? And for the Curse, Anger Management Issues, or Silver Vulnerability (increased damage and/or silver counting as a Sleeper Witness)?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of doing a line of &quot;hybrid&quot; Dynasties - A Wolf-Blooded Family/Proximus line, a Ghoul Family/Proximus line, a Demon-Blooded/Proximus line, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-05-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T23:26:17-07:00","id":1111992,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> , something like Remus Lupin from Harry Potter series? Wizard, but cursed with lycantropy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T03:16:59-07:00","id":1112027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1111992#post1111992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , something like Remus Lupin from Harry Potter series? Wizard, but cursed with lycantropy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar? (Haven't seen/read Harry Potter yet)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, they would have Werewolf-like Blessings, and the wolf skin or Anger Issues Tell from their Wolf-Blooded Lineage.<br /> <br /> Diet Uratha, Mage-style.<br /> <br /> Problem is, I don't know what other Arcana fits after Life and Spirit. I suppose I could just try out building them as alternative focused-Dynasty, and only give them two Arcana (but up to 4 dot Blessings in each).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T03:44:01-07:00","id":1112033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1112027#post1112027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Similar? (Haven't seen/read Harry Potter yet)</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to for this purpose. (But my GF would kill me if she knew I didn't recommend Harry Potter, though.)<br /> Remus Lupin (yes, his name is basically Wolfy McWolf) is both a wizard and a werewolf, but doesn't actually have any werewolf-related powers when not forcibly turned into one during the full moon, and then he's just a werewolf rather than a werewolf-wizard.<br /> <br /> Fate or Mind could work for a third Arcanum. One of the five Auspices has prophetic dreams, and some Gifts work in ways that reminds me of Fate. Many other Gifts can be used in social interactions in different ways, which makes Mind come to mind. The whole Lunacy thing could be a Mind Blessing where you impose one of the Lunacy Conditions on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:17:53-07:00","id":1112058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1112033#post1112033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate or Mind could work for a third Arcanum. One of the five Auspices has prophetic dreams, and some Gifts work in ways that reminds me of Fate. Many other Gifts can be used in social interactions in different ways, which makes Mind come to mind. The whole Lunacy thing could be a Mind Blessing where you impose one of the Lunacy Conditions on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>If any, I was probably thinking Mind, but also for the asset it would be for &quot;pack&quot; communication and coordination.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on what the Curse should be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T07:03:57-07:00","id":1119494,"title":"","content":"So, I still need to finalize the Curse on this one. And some help with familial Pack traits for the Wolf-Blooded Family side (basically, an inherited Pack bound to a Totem).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bardou</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long ago, two families of power merged their lines. One was a dynasty of shamans and weavers of Supernal magic. The other was a line of shapeshifters and their kin, bound through blood and oath to a spiritual totem. The legacy of their union is the Bardou line, keeping both the shapechanger\u2019s bonds to their totem, and their dynasty\u2019s gifts at Supernal Magic.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Bardou often have a feral mein about them, regardless of whatever other Tells they might possess. Some are more hirsute than norm, others have exaggerated canines, or a predatory gait.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nicknames:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Witch-wolves, Lupins</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Thyrsus</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessings (Life, Spirit, Mind):</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Life - Speak With Beasts \u2022, Web of Life \u2022, Control Instincts \u2022\u2022, Heightened Senses \u2022\u2022, Knit \u2022\u2022\u2022, Transform Life \u2022\u2022\u2022</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">; Spirit - Exorcist\u2019s Eye \u2022, Know Spirit \u2022, Channel Essence \u2022\u2022, Command Spirit \u2022\u2022, Place of Power \u2022\u2022\u2022, Spirit Summons \u2022\u2022\u2022; Mind - Mental Scan \u2022, Telepathy \u2022\u2022, Universal Language \u2022\u2022\u2022;</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curse:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> [Turn into violent wolf, or silver allergy? Silver is treated as a Sleeper Witness? Tell is integrated into Proximus curse?]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Persistent:</b> </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beat:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Severe:</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Gazing at the moon, Hunting, Protecting claimed territory</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Character Concepts:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Shape-shifting mage, guardian of the Gauntlet, scion of two worlds</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Family Tells:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Anger Issues, Second Skin, or Shape-Shifted</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Family Pack Traits:</b> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-23-2017, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T15:57:13-07:00","id":1122529,"title":"","content":"So, people: Ninja Proximus Dynasty. I'm thinking Death and Mind, but Space (Mastigos) or Matter (Moros)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T22:53:50-07:00","id":1122616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1122529#post1122529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, people: Ninja Proximus Dynasty. I'm thinking Death and Mind, but Space (Mastigos) or Matter (Moros)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you thinking they are more assassins or spies? If you lean towards one or the other I would decide the path that way. Spies and thieves for Mastigos and Moros for assassins. If it's an even spilt I would try to come up with a philosophy or back story for them and then just pick which path fits their mythos and methods better. If you have their arcana picked it would feel more like a flavor choice at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:26:42-07:00","id":1123222,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Masters of Coins</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This bloodline was intended to serve as stewards of Mages\u2019 material fortunes (there is some dispute whether the originators were Seers of the Throne or Silver Ladder). Blessed with talents toward accounting and keeping track of their master\u2019s possessions, they were prized servants. Until the line itself grew too large and poor decisions even clever bookkeeping couldn\u2019t solve struck. The bloodline has since branched out, and while many still find themselves serving others, a number have taken their fortunes into their own hands, for good or ill.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Innocuous, but professional attire with the faint sound of bills ruffling, or coins clicking together not matter what they actually possess.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nicknames:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Accountants, Moneymancers</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mastigos</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessings (Mind, Space, Matter):</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mind \u2013 One Mind, Two Thoughts (\u2022), Perfect Recall (\u2022), First Impressions (\u2022\u2022), Augment Mind (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Space \u2013 Correspondence (\u2022), Locate Object (\u2022), Borrow Threads (\u2022\u2022), Secret Door (\u2022\u2022), Ward (\u2022\u2022), Ban (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Co-Location (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Matter \u2013 Craftsman's Eye (\u2022), Detect Substance (\u2022), Discern Composition (\u2022), Lodestone (\u2022), Hidden Hoard (\u2022\u2022), Crucible (\u2022\u2022\u2022);</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curse:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Master of Coin see the world through the lense of material wealth, judging each based not on their own merit, but by the amount of capital they can claim.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Persistent:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A Master of Coin has their impression modified by the relative discrepancy in the Resources merit between them and their target, with wealthy individuals automatically gaining a greater impression, and poorer individuals snubbed. They can suppress this reaction by spending a Willpower point each Scene.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beat:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Whenever a financial superior exploits their altered perceptions to the Proximus's detriment.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Severe:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Master of Coin suffers from a form of the Paranoid Condition, based on suspecting others of using them, or just after their wealth/power. Additionally, the fate of their own wealth becomes inextricably tied to their spiritual reserves - as long as they suffer under the Severe form of their curse, misfortune strikes to make sure they can only access the benefit of Resources no higher than their current Mana total.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Balancing accounts, enumerating wealth, gaining capital without physical effort.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Character Concepts:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Economist, Bookie, Counterfeiter</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-31-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T18:27:44-07:00","id":1139318,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Syzygoi<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Tulpa Projectors<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Syzygoi often share physical marks and/or behavioral tics with their Goetia, whether self-inflicted or absorbed through a sort of psychic osmosis. The most common among these traits are symbolic tattoos, weirdly colored eyes, and a vague sensation that someone or something is speaking simultaneously with the Syzygos. When a Syzygos uses their Blessings to activate their Goetia, they act in harmony proportional to the stability of the Syzygos psyche. Furthermore, the Goetia of Syzygoi with more stable psyches tend to appear more well-intentioned and cognizant, but not necessarily nicer or more human.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Mastigos<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings:</b> Mind \u2013 Know Nature (1), Method Man* (1), Mental Scan (1), Perfect Recall (1), Alter Mental Pattern (2), Mental Shield (2), Telepathy (2), Augment Mind (3), Enhance Skill (3), Goetic Summons (3)<br /> <br /> Spirit \u2013 Exorcist\u2019s Eye (1), Know Spirit (1), Gossamer Touch (2), Bolster Spirit (3), Shape Spirit (4)<br /> <br /> <b>Curse: </b>The Syzygoi are metaphysically bound to abnormal Goetia that come to existence within their Oneiroi at the moment of their transformation into Proximi. While these Goetia will do their best to protect their Proximi, they are not guaranteed to share the same ideals and goals.<br /> <br /> Other traits of the Goetia:<ul><li>They are usually Rank 2, and whatever aspect(s) of the Proximus\u2019 mind they embody is not removed as a result of leaving the Oneiros.</li> <li>They do not suffer Essence Bleed, and gain their Rank per day in Essence just by being around the Syzygos.</li> <li>Once per day, if the Syzygos gains Willpower from any source other than sleeping, completes a short term Aspiration, makes progress toward a long term Aspiration or risks losing Integrity, the Goetia may roll Power or Finesse + Rank, with each Success granting one Essence (even if the roll fails, one Essence is still granted).</li> <li>They possess a Ban, Bane, Virtue, Vice and Aspirations. They cannot be removed from the Syzygos through supernatural means, although a full Awakening of the Syzygos allows separation if they so wish.</li> </ul><b>Persistent:</b> Once per scene, the ST may ask the Syzygos\u2019 player to roll Resolve + Composure with a penalty equal to [10 \u2013 Integrity]. On a Failure, the Goetia will Urge the Syzygos toward actions chosen by the ST for the rest of the scene. These actions usually involve facing the difficult or dark parts of the Syzgos' life, or taking great risks for great rewards. On a Success, the Syzygos remains in control. Furthermore, the Syzygos has the Resonant Condition for Goetia.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> When the Syzygos suffers difficulties because of disagreements with their Goetia, follows its advice without thinking too much about the consequences, or is harmed by someone taking advantage of the Goetia, take a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> The Syzygos may choose to deny the roll demanded by the Persistent Curse. Doing so upgrades the Resonant Condition to Open, or causes all damage suffered by the Goetia to also happen to the Syzygos. This lasts for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Helping someone reconcile two conflicting sides of their personality, Pit yourself against a rival, Spend precious time with someone that completes you, Investigate contradictory statements or actions, Surprise others by acting contrary to what they would expect<br /> <br /> <b>Character Concepts:</b> Badass Diplomat And Their Wise Advisor, Gifted But Eccentric Artist/Inventor And Their Sublime Muse, Two Martial Artists In One, Conflicted Revenge Seeker And Their Corrupting Teacher, A Child At Heart And Their Loyal \u201cImaginary\u201d Friend<br /> <br /> *Method Man Spell (Courstery Of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10091_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10091\" data-vbnamecard=\"10091\">Altasaire</a>):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Method Man (Mind \u2022) </b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Investigation, Athletics, Socialize<br /> <br /> It is said that a wise man wins first, and only then enters the battle, and the fool first enters the battle and only then tries to win it. It is also said that no plan survives contact with the enemy. This spell tries to rectify the latter by bolstering the subject's ability to think on the fly, expanding his mental capacity to allow him to handle small minutae on the fly, without cutting in the precious attention that is often sorely needed to handle more pressing tasks of the moment. For the duration of the spell the subject could modify any Plan-type equipment he has as per gear modification rules, treating each significant part of the plan that needs to be changed as a separate &quot;feature&quot; to be added.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell also speeds up the decision-making process considerably, allowing to make changes in the plans at the same time as performing another, separate instant or extended task.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>Perception of the subject is sharpened to a needle point, as the world around slows to a seeming crawl. He can create a whole new plan on the spot rather than modifying an existing one while the spell is in effect at the same time as performing another instant or extended task.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T01:41:27-07:00","id":1139381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1112058#post1112058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on what the Curse should be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is long overdue, but I have a suggestion for the Bardou. What if their Dynasty's Curse is tied strongly to their family's bond to the Totem? I know conventional packs have to live adhering to the Bans of their own spirit patrons.<br /> <br /> That said, would the Wolf-Blooded family's Totem perhaps be an ancestor spirit? Or perhaps it's one of the wolf spirits tied to a Firstborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T10:57:32-07:00","id":1139485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1139381#post1139381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is long overdue, but I have a suggestion for the Bardou. What if their Dynasty's Curse is tied strongly to their family's bond to the Totem? I know conventional packs have to live adhering to the Bans of their own spirit patrons.<br /> <br /> That said, would the Wolf-Blooded family's Totem perhaps be an ancestor spirit? Or perhaps it's one of the wolf spirits tied to a Firstborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need the help of someone more versed in Werewolf for that component.<br /> <br /> The Bardou are super cursed - they have the Proximus Curse, Tell, and Totem Ban to manage.<br /> <br /> Tentative history is a marriage of alliance between a familial Proximus Dynasty and a Wolf-blooded lineage. Eventually, crap happened and majorly depopulated the local Uratha, leaving the line to manage the local Shadow.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they were Mages cursed [insert folklore-ish origin for werewolves] to become wolves, and whose powers have since adapted/decayed. (For settings that don't want to include Uratha. Yet use the mechanics for some reason).<br /> <br /> Issue is a Curse that doesn't overlap with the Tell curses - rage, silver, the moon, etc. Unless... I make the Tell curses trigger the Proximus Curse (and vice a versa)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T11:08:34-07:00","id":1139489,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm almost done with the first &quot;ninja&quot; Dynasty I'm working on (the Moros/Assassin one). Tentatively working on a supporting merit that let's them treat a slain foe as a Sleepwalker for the purposes of spell control as long as it is undetected.<br /> <br /> Second one is more spy focused and Mastigos based.<br /> <br /> And I hope to have a related Pirate one (Death, Matter, Mind or Space) ready for talk-like-a-pirate day. (With a similar Merit, but using treasure/Resources for support - to encourage buried treasure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T01:22:05-07:00","id":1139658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1139489#post1139489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm almost done with the first &quot;ninja&quot; Dynasty I'm working on (the Moros/Assassin one). Tentatively working on a supporting merit that let's them treat a slain foe as a Sleepwalker for the purposes of spell control as long as it is undetected.<br /> <br /> Second one is more spy focused and Mastigos based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember them to connect to Guardians 'protection' of Dynasty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1139489#post1139489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I hope to have a related Pirate one (Death, Matter, Mind or Space) ready for talk-like-a-pirate day. (With a similar Merit, but using treasure/Resources for support - to encourage buried treasure).</div> </div> </div> </div>And those will have strong ties in Free Council. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T02:57:30-07:00","id":1139666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1139658#post1139658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember them to connect to Guardians 'protection' of Dynasty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And those will have strong ties in Free Council. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I try to treat Proximus Dynasties as separate/independent as possible, so I don't reference Order allegiance much, leaving it open.<br /> <br /> But if you want, the associations are easy enough to draw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T10:13:23-07:00","id":1139962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1139485#post1139485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Issue is a Curse that doesn't overlap with the Tell curses - rage, silver, the moon, etc. Unless... I make the Tell curses trigger the Proximus Curse (and vice a versa)...</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a prohibition against kinslaying? To reflect one tenet in the Oath of the Moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T11:35:08-07:00","id":1401939,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><u>The scions of Midas</u></b><br /> <br /> The proud heirs of Midas claim the story of their mythic patriarch is a actually an allegory, they say Midas offered hospitality to an archmage (or a supernal god, even amongst the line the identiy of Dionysus isn't all clear) and in return for it, Midas was blessed and granted proximus status.<br /> His ability to turn everything he touched into gold was actually a reference to his prolific use of his Stealing Fire prime blessing, when after multiple use of the spell on his daughter broke her soul, another ascended being punished the King by giving him donkey ears so that any who could see the Truth would know of his shame, again the bloodline records aren't clear on who or what this ascended being was and multiple legends around the world describe several kings with donkey ears, making some think that this dynasty has been around even before the Fall.<br /> <br /> Today, the Scion of Midas are under the protection of the Silver Ladder, well for the most part, the Chancellor servant and the Paternoster ministry don't hesitate to &quot;poach&quot; potential proximi from the Silver Ladder.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Scions, Golden Kings/Queens, Mules (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Most of the Scions come from money, they are usually well dressed and usually of <span style=\"font-family:DDG_ProximaNova, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_0, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_1, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_2, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_3, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_4, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_5, DDG_ProximaNova_UI_6, Proxima Nova, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Segoe UI, Nimbus Sans L, Liberation Sans, Open Sans, FreeSans, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Mediterranean descent but the line has spread far an wide and modern kings and queens can look like anything. Regardless of their gender, most Scions wear extensive jewelry, usually made from gold, as they remind them of their kingly heritage and complement their ego, all member of the line are very self conscious about their look and work a great deal to keep a somewhat attractive physics, some physical traits like buck teeth or a fine coat of hair on the back and torso oddly reminiscent of donkey fur has been known to manifest as some proximi develop their blessings, usually to the great shame of the scion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings:</b> Prime-- Word of Command \u2022, Pierce Deception \u2022, Word of Truth \u2022\u2022, Aetheric Winds \u2022\u2022\u2022, Stealing Fire \u2022\u2022\u2022. Forces -- Kinetic Efficiency \u2022, Influence Fire \u2022, Control Fire \u2022\u2022, Environmental Shield \u2022\u2022, Call Lightning \u2022\u2022\u2022, Telekinesis \u2022\u2022\u2022 Matter-- Detect Substance \u2022, Craftsman\u2019s Eye \u2022, Shaping \u2022\u2022, Hidden Hoard \u2022\u2022, Crucible \u2022\u2022\u2022, Nigredo and Albedo \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Curse: </b>The Scions of Midas are ever prideful of their blessings and ever foolish in their uses<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent :</b> The Dynasty know that their heritage makes them special but despite appearances, they are deeply insecure about it, any rolls made to make fun or try to shut down a scion gain the 8 again quality.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> the Scion loose her temper in public, takes on a task that she's not qualified to take on or get made fun of or shut down in public or making a fool of themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe:</b> Invoking Paradox is a failure on the Scion part, they gain the Guilty condition that any mage or supernal entity can exploit, this condition only goes away after makings amends or sucking it up to another mage, even if they did not wrong any mages, their failure to properly use their gift is a blemish on the scion bloodline and a reminder of the foolishness of their Patriarch. sometime the supernal forces that be seem to add insult to injury by granting the scion horses or donkey's ear clearly visible to anyone who can see past the Lie.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Acquiring or working with Gold, Making a good impression at a social event, acting as a judge during a contest, offerings to Pan, Dionysus or Appollo.<br /> <br /> <b>Character concepts</b> : Trustfund College Kid, Jeweler, Mage's personal herald, Narcissistic Politician.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T13:39:54-07:00","id":1403150,"title":"","content":"<u><b>The Eyes in the Crowd</b></u><br /> <br /> This Proximus dynasty is very valued by both the Guardians and the Panopticon Ministry because of their natural talents for spying. Unfortunately, their interest isn't mutual. The Faceless want nothing more but to be left alone to their own devices; they barely tolerate each other and the competitive environment of an average Consilium or Tetrarchy drives them crazy. They did everything they could to disappear from the surface of Earth, to the point where most mages who know about this dynasty consider it extinct.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Hermits<br /> <b>Appearance: </b>They tend to be nondescript, to the point their faces are hard to remember. They are neither ugly nor beautiful and their features are never unusual for their ethnic background. They even have no birthmarks and the more clever Hermits actually add some to look less suspicious.<br /> <b>Parent Path: </b>Mastigos<br /> <b>Blessings: (Mind, Space, Death): </b>Mind <b>\u2013 </b>Know Nature (*), Incognito Presence (**), Memory Hole (**), Imposter (***), Sleep of the Just (***); Space \u2013 Isolation (*), The Outward and Inward Eye (*), Break Boundary (**), Scrying (**), Veil Sympathy (**), Ward (**), Ban (***); Death: Deepen Shadows (*), Shadow Sculpting (*), Suppress Aura (**), Without a Trace (**)<br /> <b>Curse: </b>The Eyes are all about observing people from the shadows, never mingling with them. Not only they don't like it \u2013 but prolonged attention weakens the magic that lets the Hermits hide in plain sight. For that reasons, they spend a lot of time alone; they rarely even form familial units, which makes it hard to propagate the bloodline further.<br /> <b>Persistent: </b>Whenever a Hermit tries Social Maneuvering, people find it hard to pay attention to them: they always have to open one more Door to get through the wall of indifference. They also suffer a penalty: -1 to all Social Maneuvering rolls.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Whenever the Eye misses an opportunity associated with a social interaction, take a Beat.<br /> <b>Severe: </b>If the Proximus gets a lot of attention for a prolonged time, or uses magic to make themselves more noticeable, the curse deepens. In addition to the Persistent effects, they become more ugly and off-putting: their Impression starts one step lower than it normally would and can never be raised to Perfect. Every failed Social Maneuvering roll becomes a Dramatic Failure. The only way to end the curse is to spend at least several days in complete solitude \u2013 even seeing another person resets the counter.<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Watching people without being seen, meditating in solitude.<br /> <b>Character Concepts: </b>Reclusive social sciences professor, reluctant spy, elusive assassin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","name":"Gantolandon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T19:20:28-07:00","id":1403169,"title":"","content":"I'm very sorry, but I have a question for this thread rather than a Dynasty to add (i have yet to tread the game besides basic lore).<br /> <br /> How do dynasties work in their relationship with Orders? Can they be tied with them while others try and remain separate? Is this why dynasties can &quot;belong&quot; to both Pentacle and Seer Orders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T14:11:09-07:00","id":1403287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1403169#post1403169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very sorry, but I have a question for this thread rather than a Dynasty to add (i have yet to tread the game besides basic lore).<br /> <br /> How do dynasties work in their relationship with Orders? Can they be tied with them while others try and remain separate? Is this why dynasties can &quot;belong&quot; to both Pentacle and Seer Orders?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tied to Pentacle or Seer Orders, not and, I think. That said, yes, some Proximi dynasties probably do try to steer clear of the Orders and have a Nameless Order of their own functioning around their members who manage to Awaken. The Silver Ladder in particular take a custodial role around Proximi, and depending on the Caucus this can be pretty good, or out and out eugenics. The relationships are often complex though. Like, the Myrmidons serve the Praetorians, but they maintain their own private cults and secrets that they won't surrender to the Praetorians even at the cost of their souls and lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T16:06:01-07:00","id":1403299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1403287#post1403287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tied to Pentacle or Seer Orders, not and, I think. That said, yes, some Proximi dynasties probably do try to steer clear of the Orders and have a Nameless Order of their own functioning around their members who manage to Awaken. The Silver Ladder in particular take a custodial role around Proximi, and depending on the Caucus this can be pretty good, or out and out eugenics. The relationships are often complex though. Like, the Myrmidons serve the Praetorians, but they maintain their own private cults and secrets that they won't surrender to the Praetorians even at the cost of their souls and lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, if I may ask one more question, what is the &quot;parent path&quot; lore wise? I understand it has to due mostly with thematics and such, but does it simply mean that they are &quot;in tune&quot; with certain Paths more than others? Or is a dynasty with Moros as its origin destined to Awaken as a Moros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T17:34:57-07:00","id":1403443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1403299#post1403299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, if I may ask one more question, what is the &quot;parent path&quot; lore wise? I understand it has to due mostly with thematics and such, but does it simply mean that they are &quot;in tune&quot; with certain Paths more than others? Or is a dynasty with Moros as its origin destined to Awaken as a Moros?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mostly thematics. The Sisters of the Mountain are in tune with the Thyrsus Path, so their Blessings are Life and Spirit oriented, along with Fate. Even their curse is thematically tied to Life. They're more likely to Awaken as Thyrsus, but they are not required to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T17:46:50-07:00","id":1403444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023190-homebrew-proximi-dynasties?p=1403443#post1403443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's mostly thematics. The Sisters of the Mountain are in tune with the Thyrsus Path, so their Blessings are Life and Spirit oriented, along with Fate. Even their curse is thematically tied to Life. They're more likely to Awaken as Thyrsus, but they are not required to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thank you. Hopefully I'll one day have the confidence to write a dynasty, but for now I'm just happy reading what yall have. It's very fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T01:38:04-07:00","id":1403497,"title":"","content":"Lorewise it could mean that each Dynasty is connected to one of the five Supernal Realms/Watchtowers, just like the five Paths. So less an actual &quot;parent&quot; Path so much as drawing from the same sources as one.<br /> But that's just a theory and I have no text to back it up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}